{"id": "whdonana", "name": "Doñana National Park", "short": "Doñana", "place": "Andalusia, Spain", "lat": 37.0, "lon": -6.4, "side": "l", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Spain", "kind": "Lakes & wetlands", "park": true, "blurb": "Marsh, lynx and rabbits: a flooded delta on the African-European flyway.", "tip": {"id": "rabbit", "title": "Crash the rabbits", "text": "Rabbits are the main food of the lynx and imperial eagle. Set European rabbit to -100% and watch the lynx, then the eagle, mongooses and genets switch to other prey."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Doñana National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doñana_National_Park"}, {"title": "UNESCO World Heritage: Doñana National Park", "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/685/"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Iberian lynx", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iberian_lynx"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Spanish imperial eagle", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_imperial_eagle"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: European rabbit", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_rabbit"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Greater flamingo", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_flamingo"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Doñana National Park", "icon": "water", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "cork", "sp": "quercus suber", "xh": 0.12}, {"id": "rockrose", "sp": "cistus salviifolius", "xh": 0.35}, {"id": "clubrush", "sp": "bolboschoenus maritimus", "xh": 0.6, "desc": "A sedge of the brackish and freshwater marsh edges that grows where the marisma floods.", "ic": "grass"}, {"id": "algae", "sp": "bacillariophyta", "xh": 0.85}, {"id": "rabbit", "sp": "oryctolagus cuniculus", "xh": 0.05, "desc": "Grazes grasses and shoots and is the staple food of the Iberian lynx and Spanish imperial eagle. Disease has cut its numbers badly.", "ic": "vole", "badge": "Keystone grazer"}, {"id": "reddeer", "sp": "cervus elaphus", "xh": 0.19, "name": "Red deer", "wiki": "Red deer", "desc": "Large grazer and browser of the scrub and woodland, and the most recorded mammal in the GBIF data around the park.", "ic": "elk"}, {"id": "fallow", "sp": "dama dama", "xh": 0.33}, {"id": "boar", "sp": "sus scrofa", "xh": 0.47, "name": "Wild boar", "desc": "A versatile omnivore that digs roots, eats acorns and seeds, and also takes small animals and carrion."}, {"id": "crayfish", "sp": "procambarus clarkii", "xh": 0.62}, {"id": "coot", "sp": "fulica atra", "xh": 0.76, "desc": "An abundant marsh bird and a staple of the winter waterfowl crowds, taken by eagles and other predators."}, {"id": "flamingo", "sp": "phoenicopterus roseus", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "Stirs up shallow mud and filters out small crustaceans, algae, seeds and larvae. Seen in large numbers on the marisma."}, {"id": "mongoose", "sp": "herpestes ichneumon", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "genet", "sp": "genetta genetta", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "A small night-hunting carnivore that takes rodents, rabbits, birds and reptiles. The Iberian lynx often kills genets."}, {"id": "otter", "sp": "lutra lutra", "xh": 0.55, "desc": "Eats mainly fish, plus amphibians, crustaceans and waterbirds. Here that includes coots and the introduced crayfish."}, {"id": "heron", "sp": "ardea cinerea", "xh": 0.75, "desc": "A wading bird of the marshes that eats fish, frogs and crayfish. The park holds one of the largest heronries in the Mediterranean."}, {"id": "stork", "sp": "ciconia ciconia", "xh": 0.92}, {"id": "lynx", "sp": "lynx pardinus", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "eagle", "sp": "aquila adalberti", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Hot dry summers set the Mediterranean rhythm of growth in the scrub and woodland."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "autumn-winter rain", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "flood", "sp": "marisma flooding", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": 